172:             "revised_operationalization": "1. Fisher logs the catch on a daily sheet that shows the net used, the quantity taken (must be \u22641 unit), and a note that any excess fish were released.  The fisher signs the sheet and a nearby community member signs as witness.\n2. On the weekly council meeting, the council member collects fines from those who exceeded the quota and records each fine in the shared ledger.  The council member also reviews the daily logs and may randomly audit a few trips, asking the fisher to demonstrate the release of excess fish or to provide a photo.\n3. The fisher who has performed community service signs a community\u2011service log that lists the date, activity, and hours spent.\n4. The council member reviews the service log, asks a short verification question, and records the service entry in the shared ledger under the fisher\u2019s name.\n5. Random audits may be conducted by a council member or appointed verifier to ensure compliance with both the quota and the service requirement.  If a fisher fails to provide a signed log or is found to have violated the quota, the fine is doubled and an extra day of community service is added.  All audit findings are recorded in the shared ledger for transparency."
